00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.390
Kurashiki Community Pool

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.390
Day of the Match

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:20.020
Right here--left wing is Amihama.
Use your speed to frazzle the enemy.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:25.820
Ejiri is left flat. He'll use his arm
to take open shots.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:31.950
Babayaro and his long limbs will play
floater back, focusing on defense.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:36.790
I'll play right flat and
pass the ball around.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:41.500
Right wing is Ushimado.
Don't let the enemy through.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:45.880
Lastly, Minato will be our floater.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:50.220
As the core of the offense,
floaters score points.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:53.390
So get the ball to Minato-<i>senpai</i>!

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:54.980
Everyone on board?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.100
--Yeah
--Yes.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.810
As long as we win.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.360
Agreed.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:05.190
This match might revive
the player you used to be!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.650
I wonder.

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:11.080
Dude, anyone else dig these chocolates?

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.370
Mmm!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.240
Thank goodness!

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.540
You made 'em?

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:22.130
Yeah. I read that chocolate is good
for energy right before a match.

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:24.510
It's true! I feel charged up!

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.010
Really?

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:32.300
Let's make it a tradition to have
Babi's sweets before a match!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.270
--Yeah!
--Oh, look, they're eating!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:39.100
Let's hope you don't barf
during the match.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.480
Who are you?

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:43.650
Hmm? Holy bangs!

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:47.240
These are our opponents from Rikka Gakuen!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.700
--Eh?
--Huh?

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:51.740
Not Shogakukan?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:56.450
You think you can take on Shogaku?
You'd get slaughtered.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:57.580
Eh?!

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.960
Stop, Toyama.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:02.920
I'm the captain, Fukui. Hello, again.

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.420
Hello.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:07.880
Our good neighbors suggested
a practice match.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.090
Rikka Gakuen...

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:10.930
Yes.

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:13.930
The one with junior high water polo?

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:17.560
Correct. It's a combined campus.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.270
With an incredibly weak team.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.320
I didn't play water polo
because there were

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:29.950
only two schools in
the prefecture with it.

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:33.990
The one he didn't attend
had an awful team.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:38.660
Your team was so bad,
I had to give up trying to beat him.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.410
The hell--?!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:44.460
It's true. Their high school
boys' team has never won.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:45.420
Eh?

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:46.630
Oh, wow.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:50.550
Don't underestimate us!
We're not as weak as you think!

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:53.970
We're Rikka Gakuen's best--
the "Hokuriku Three"!

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:55.010
Eh?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.680
"Hokuriku Three"?

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.810
Don't, Toyama.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:01.310
Doesn't the trash talk
piss you off, Ishikawa?

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:05.900
Oh! 'Cuz you're Toyama,
Ishikawa, and Fukui?

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.780
--Ah!
--Oh!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.190
What's so funny?!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:12.030
Sorry!

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.950
I said not to call us that!

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.120
Who cares about that?!

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:21.620
Where's the rest of your team?

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.420
Everyone suddenly fell sick.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:25.710
Eh?

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.090
So... today's match...

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:29.880
Excuse us!

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:32.420
Phew! We made it in time!

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.630
Welcome.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:36.390
It's been a while, Aki! Is your mom well?

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:37.420
Of course.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.060
Nice!

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:39.220
Thanks for coming.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:45.190
Your four day notice didn't give
us much time to prepare!

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:45.190
Four days?!

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:50.940
Ah... The Mizushima Junior Team
will be playing in our place.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.820
Good luck today!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:55.240
Good luck.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:59.080
Good... luck.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.540
Did you plan for this from the start?

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.370
Of course not.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.080
Yamanami High School

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.080
Mizushima Junior Team

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.190
Why aren't you playing?

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.240
We were going to when you suggested it,

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:41.830
but our first victory may ride
on not showing our hand.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:47.710
Never thought you'd care
about Yamanami, Chinu.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:55.260
I'm just curious to see
Minato Kiyomizu play.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:20:02.260
I can't wait to see who's the weaker
team between them and us.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:04.640
You don't look excited.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:10.730
Anyway, it doesn't seem like Kiyomizu
remembers playing against us.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.450
Grade schoolers sure are small.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:27.620
Still, this is a new start for me.
I'm not gonna hold back!

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:33.710
Both teams rush to get the ball at the
start, so the fastest swimmer gets it.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:38.510
We have Amihama,
so it'll be ours for sure.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.970
It's all you, Amiami!

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.360
It's ours! Good!

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.950
I'm in position!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.910
Nice! And now the shot!

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.210
Ours!

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:18.340
Free shot!

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:40.200
Shit!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.200
Well, well.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:47.120
--Nice shot!
--Good one!
--Keep it up!

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.840
This ain't looking good.
